94c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress (2026-11-19 PST): implemented per the signed plan; commit eafd914081e on a fresh worktree from origin/main, make verify running. New tests/unit/reconciler/test_create_writes_not_replayed.py (15 tests) failed 13/15 before the fix (the 2 passing are the unchanged-behaviour guards: Cloud 429 retry, DC read retry) and pass after. Library check: uv.lock pins jira 3.10.5; its source shows ResilientSession re-sends any method on requests ConnectionError and makes exactly 1 attempt at max_retries=0, and create_issue(prefetch=False) skips the follow-up GET. Not tested against the real library (not installed in any test tier). A broad local run of tests/unit/reconciler under -n 4 on a loaded host had 3 lock-ref test failures (test_lock_orphan_local_ref.py, state/test_ref_lock.py); they passed 23/23 in isolation and do not touch the changed files; make verify is the arbiter.","timestamp":1795153034942079001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify via verify-slot.sh (outside the sandbox; an earlier sandboxed run lost PyPI access and an earlier slot run was stopped by the coordinator): 21549 passed, 1 failed = tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py::test_resign_makes_enforced_verify_pass_with_era_keys, red on the base commit and fixed on origin/main by 2825b4fe283 (gloomful-genial-pronghorn). Pushed as Gerrit change 3486 (patch set 1, eafd914081e).","timestamp":1795203784001061001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3486 merged as 904de16194b48a461271e4e160fdd96fffb1c88c (2026-11-20 14:52 PST), on origin/main. Patch set 1 (eafd914081e): LLM-Review +1, Verified -1 only from tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py, red on its parent and fixed on main by 2825b4fe283. Patch set 2 (2a827ee8368): rebased on origin/main and adds test_the_mapping_probe_honours_a_429_retry_after for the review advisory (it fails when the probe's rate_limit_retry opt-in is removed); make verify passed (21577 passed + 226 integration, 0 failed); LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved. AC evidence: Cloud comment create -> test_a_failed_cloud_comment_create_is_not_replayed (+429 still retried); DC create -> test_a_dc_create_that_may_have_landed_is_sent_once (3 fault types, raises builtin ConnectionError/TimeoutError) and test_a_lost_dc_create_is_recovered_by_label_not_replayed; DC comment -> test_a_dc_comment_that_may_have_landed_is_sent_once; max_retries=0 -> test_the_dc_client_is_built_without_library_retries. Accepted behaviour change (in plan): DC writes no longer get the jira library's hidden 429/5xx retry. Unverified: real jira library behaviour under max_retries=0 (source-read for 3.10.5, not installed in any test tier); no live DC instance exercised.","timestamp":1795215292958342001}],"created_at":1795095285409670521,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"66361f40-e117-47a1-8405-f7fed578d436","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7bed-62ad-fbc3-462f"},{"link_uuid":"26ea6473-8504-4808-a723-539a639890eb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"},{"link_uuid":"01c15ab8-0286-4af1-a70a-5bab981393b5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a78d-e995-43c9-4498"},{"link_uuid":"4e592368-0ce3-40f1-b632-ce7be0af5088","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0628-9d41-0e80-481b"}],"description":"## Observation (from code, 2026-11-19 PST)\n`highbred-fabled-lobo` (Gerrit 3452, fa383b1d195) stopped the Cloud ACLI transport from re-running `jira workitem create` after a non-zero exit, because the create may already have landed. The code review of that change named 2 sibling paths with the same shape; neither is changed there:\n- Data Center: `_IssuesMixin.create_issue` (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`) wraps the REST create in `_with_connection_retry`, which re-runs it on connection faults, including a fault after the request was sent.\n- Cloud comments: `_NON_REPLAYABLE_COMMANDS` in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` lists only `jira workitem create`, so `jira workitem comment create` is still retried after any non-zero exit and can post a duplicate comment.\n\nNot established: whether either path has produced a duplicate in production. That needs a search of the Jira project for duplicate issues created seconds apart, and for repeated comments.\n\n### Further observation (from code and library source, 2026-11-19 PST)\n- The Data Center client is built by `build_client_from_settings` (`jira_datacenter/transport.py`) as `jira.JIRA(server=..., token_auth=..., options=...)` with no `max_retries`. In `jira` 3.8, `JIRA.__init__` defaults `max_retries=3` and sets it on its `ResilientSession`, whose `request` loop treats every `requests` `ConnectionError` as recoverable for any HTTP method, POST included. So a DC create or comment POST is re-sent inside the library before rebar's own `_with_connection_retry` sees the fault, and rebar then re-runs the whole call.\n- `jira.JIRA.create_issue` defaults `prefetch=True`: after the POST it issues a GET for the new issue inside the same call. Callers read only `key` and `id` from the result.\n- The create coordinator already has the recovery path for an ambiguous create: `_CoordinatedSeams.create_execute` (`create_route.py`) maps builtin `TimeoutError` and `ConnectionError` to `timeout`/`connection_lost`, then `observe` finds a landed issue by its `rebar-id:` label and binds it, or defers the create as `commit_unknown`. A `requests` `ConnectionError`/`ReadTimeout` is not a builtin `ConnectionError`/`TimeoutError`; today it becomes a `permanent` create failure.\n- Outbound comments are deduplicated next pass by body equality (`outbound_comments.py`).\n- Library calls not routed through `_with_connection_retry` today: the client constructor (its default `get_server_info=True` sends a GET), `mapping_probe._JiraProbePort` reads, `backend._search_users_by_username`, and the Epic Link `fields()` lister in `_hierarchy.py`.\n\n## Approach\nExtend the existing \"never replay a create\" rule from `highbred-fabled-lobo` to the remaining create-type writes, and hand ambiguous DC outcomes to the coordinator's existing label-observe path. No config key, env var or flag; the behaviour is unconditional.\n1. Cloud comment create: add `(\"jira\", \"workitem\", \"comment\", \"create\")` to `_NON_REPLAYABLE_COMMANDS` in `acli_subprocess.py`. `_run_acli` raises on the first non-zero exit for it, except a detected 429, which keeps its retry exactly as the issue create does.\n2. DC create-type writes: `_with_connection_retry` gains a keyword `replayable: bool = True`. With `replayable=False`, any connection fault (`requests` `ConnectionError`/`Timeout`, builtin `TimeoutError`) is raised on the first attempt with no retry; a fault that is not already a builtin `ConnectionError`/`TimeoutError` is re-raised as a builtin `ConnectionError` chained to the original, so `create_execute` classifies it `connection_lost` and runs its label observe. TLS and HTTP-error branches are unchanged. `create_issue` calls `self._client.create_issue(prefetch=False, **fields)` with `replayable=False`, so the non-replayable unit is the single POST; `add_comment` passes `replayable=False`.\n3. DC library layer: `build_client_from_settings` passes `max_retries=0`, so rebar's `_with_connection_retry` is the only retry layer. The reads that bypassed it are wrapped so they keep a connection-fault retry: the client constructor (retried as a read inside `build_client_from_settings`), `_JiraProbePort` (built by `build_probe` with a call wrapper that routes each read through `_with_connection_retry(rate_limit_retry=True)`), `_search_users_by_username`, and the `fields()` lister.\n4. Intended consequence for DC writes: they also lose the library's hidden retry of 429 responses and of 503 responses with `Retry-After`. That matches rebar's documented DC policy that mutations fail on the first 429 (`retry.py`; `test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py`); a throttled write fails that mutation and the next pass retries it. Reads lose only the library's 503 and header-less 429 retries; rebar's opted-in 429 retry stays.\nNot changed: DC and Cloud link create, which link two existing issues rather than create a record.\nPortability: no process, signal, path or encoding change.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/`: `retry.py`, `transport.py`, `_issues.py`, `_links.py`, `_hierarchy.py`, `backend.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/mapping_probe.py`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_create_writes_not_replayed.py` (new).\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_pat_required.py`: its fake constructor takes a fixed `(server, token_auth, options)` signature and must accept `max_retries`.\n\n## Testing\nNew `tests/unit/reconciler/test_create_writes_not_replayed.py`, written first and seen failing before the fix:\n- Cloud comment: a fake ACLI records each `jira workitem comment create` and exits non-zero; `add_comment` raises and exactly 1 record exists. A 429 on the first comment create is retried and ends with 1 recorded comment.\n- DC create and DC comment: a fake client records the call, then raises a connection fault; `create_issue`/`add_comment` raise a builtin `ConnectionError` and the fake records exactly 1 call. Run for builtin `TimeoutError` (unit tier) and for `requests` `ConnectionError` and `ReadTimeout`.\n- DC create passes `prefetch=False` to the client.\n- End to end: `_coordinated_create_core` over the DC transport with a fake client whose create records the issue then raises a `requests`-style connection fault, and whose label search returns the landed issue: 1 create call, and the issue is bound (not a hard error).\n- DC reads unchanged: `get_issue` still retries a connection fault (3 attempts).\n- Library layer: `build_client_from_settings` passes `max_retries=0` and retries a constructor connection fault; `_JiraProbePort` from `build_probe` retries a read connection fault; `_search_users_by_username` and the `fields()` lister retry a connection fault.\n- Existing DC retry, Cloud create and mapping-probe tests stay green.\nNot testable here: the real `jira` library is not installed in any test tier, so the effect of `max_retries=0` on `ResilientSession` rests on the library source, not on a test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Each of the 2 paths either no longer replays a write that may have landed (verified by a regression test that fails the first attempt after the write is recorded and asserts one result), or is shown with evidence to be safe.\n- [x] Cloud `jira workitem comment create` runs once after a non-zero exit that is not a 429, verified by a regression test.\n- [x] DC `create_issue` sends one create after a connection fault and raises a builtin `ConnectionError`, verified by a regression test.\n- [x] DC `add_comment` sends one comment after a connection fault, verified by a regression test.\n- [x] The DC client is built with `max_retries=0`, verified by a construction test.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/reconciler` passes.\n- [x] `make verify` passes.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"comment create is non-replayable"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py","reason":"replayable keyword; ambiguous fault re-raised as builtin ConnectionError"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","reason":"max_retries=0; constructor retried"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","reason":"create_issue prefetch=False, not replayed"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_links.py","reason":"add_comment not replayed"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py","reason":"fields() lister retried"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"user search retried"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/mapping_probe.py","reason":"probe reads through retry wrapper"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_create_writes_not_replayed.py","reason":"new regression tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_pat_required.py","reason":"fake client ctor accepts max_retries"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0628-9d41-0e80-481b"],["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"],["relates_to","a78d-e995-43c9-4498"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"43d7234d-7db7-46d6-8179-b6b68c172fea","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge"],"ticket_id":"0e48-b2df-17eb-407d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira writes that create something are still replayed after an ambiguous failure: DC create on connection faults, ACLI comment create","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dc95205a-f1e8-48d1-9b0f-5794128361cb","d6c2ffd2-7265-45d5-80b4-96750a9a816a","26ea6473-8504-4808-a723-539a639890eb","0bbf94a3-bd4f-40f9-b0b4-3df8e33a7529","42edb105-5599-49c8-b47c-06ceeec9cdb5","e025fcf9-cb6b-40ee-a786-5b818ed9bf17","3af1d6e6-9cbe-4c03-9ce4-c67cd5614697","43d7234d-7db7-46d6-8179-b6b68c172fea","6652d308-7808-4f03-9e95-f69e00ab608f","ef2c4df3-7151-4af8-9ad0-4997f01a5552","9458b9f8-3673-41dc-b512-5964f8607fcc","01c15ab8-0286-4af1-a70a-5bab981393b5","4e592368-0ce3-40f1-b632-ce7be0af5088","e21bfe02-6f6c-410d-afc1-50174bdf4214","acf45951-d053-47ee-ad07-190b2bd29bc5"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795215292958342002,"uuid":"6d7cdc32-c655-4bf5-995d-f4a391ddfb63"}